# Every setting the server reads from its environment. Copy to .env (git-ignored) to use them on this Mac: ./start.sh and
# ./host.sh load it. A cloud host takes the same names as environment variables, with the secrets in its secret store.
# All optional: with none set, the app runs as it always has, on http://127.0.0.1:8000. docs/SECURITY.md has the checklist.

# Where it listens. 127.0.0.1 (this Mac only) by default; a container needs 0.0.0.0. Cloud Run and most hosts set PORT.
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PORT=8000

# The address people open, when the site is behind a proxy. It is the OAuth redirect base
# (<PUBLIC_URL>/api/auth/oauth/<provider>/callback); when it is https, cookies are Secure and HSTS is sent even if the
# proxy passes requests on as plain http; and its host name is added to ALLOWED_HOSTS.
# PUBLIC_URL=https://sudarshana.example.com

# The Host names the server answers to; any other gets a 400 (this stops DNS rebinding). "*.x" is any subdomain of x.
# Default: this Mac and the Cloudflare quick tunnel.
# ALLOWED_HOSTS=127.0.0.1,localhost,*.trycloudflare.com

# (uvicorn) The proxies whose X-Forwarded-For and X-Forwarded-Proto are believed: they give the client's real address,
# which the limits on wrong passwords and sign-ups count by, and whether it came over https. The default fits cloudflared
# on this Mac. On a cloud host, list its proxy's addresses or ranges. Never "*": uvicorn then takes the first
# X-Forwarded-For entry, which the client writes itself, so the per-address limits could be dodged.
# FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS=127.0.0.1,::1

# The accounts, with their saved charts, life facts and shares (SQLite). Put it on a persistent, backed-up disk.
# ACCOUNTS_DB=/var/lib/sudarshana/accounts.db

# The admin account's seed: a username, the email's SHA-256 and a scrypt hash of the password, never the real ones.
# Default server/owner.json. Read only while the database has no admin yet; a cloud host can mount it as a secret file.
# OWNER_FILE=/run/secrets/owner.json

# Sign in with a provider: each one is on once both of its values are set. Register a web app with the provider, with
# <PUBLIC_URL>/api/auth/oauth/<name>/callback as its redirect URI (for Google on this Mac:
# http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/oauth/google/callback) and the scopes in server/auth.py PROVIDERS. Secrets never go in git.
# OAUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# OAUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
# OAUTH_MICROSOFT_ID=
# OAUTH_MICROSOFT_SECRET=
# OAUTH_FACEBOOK_ID=
# OAUTH_FACEBOOK_SECRET=
# OAUTH_LINKEDIN_ID=
# OAUTH_LINKEDIN_SECRET=
